Hi Daniel. I think the functions you wrote will serve my purposes beautifully. Thanks so much!

I'm not sure how to explain the ghost of previous functions in my code if they never existed. I did publish the results from that analysis, and the code I shared is the code that was archived for that study. Additionally, I have a vague memory of my co-worker discovering those functions and pointing them out to me. So, I'm not sure how all this is possible if those functions never existed. I am seeing Nimble version 0.12.1 listed in the supplementary materials for that paper.

I got a bit of a discrepancy between values calculated from your function and those calculated manually from inside the Nimble model. Here is the relevant code:

### Your function ###

logdens.gamma <- nimbleFunction(
    run = function(x = double(), a = double(), b = double()) {
        lp <- dgamma(x, a, b, log = TRUE)
        returnType(double())
        return(lp)
    }
)

### GOF code in my model ###
## For this code, 'Traffic[j]' are the data values representing the dependent variable for this model.
 ...
    Traffic_DOY_mn[j] ~ dgamma(shape.Traffic_DOY_mn, rate.Traffic_DOY_mn[j])
    log(pred.Traffic_DOY_mn[j]) <- BETA0.Traffic_DOY_mn +
      BETA.TrailTotm.Traffic_DOY_mn * X.beta[ind.DOY_Speed[j], ind.TrailTotm] +
      BETA.RoadTotm.Traffic_DOY_mn * X.beta[ind.DOY_Speed[j], ind.RoadTotm] +
      BETA.Prp_MotRestricted.Traffic_DOY_mn * X.beta[ind.DOY_Speed[j], ind.Prp_MotRestricted] +
      BETA.Prp_HorseRestricted.Traffic_DOY_mn * X.beta[ind.DOY_Speed[j], ind.Prp_HorseRestricted]
    rate.Traffic_DOY_mn[j] <- shape.Traffic_DOY_mn / pred.Traffic_DOY_mn[j]

    #_____ GOF _____#
    LLobs.Traffic_function[j] <- logdens.gamma(Traffic[j], shape.Traffic, rate.Traffic[j]) # Log-likelihood using your function
    LLobs.Traffic_manual[j] <- log((pow(rate.Traffic[j], shape.Traffic) * # My manual calculation of log-likelihood
      Traffic[j] * exp(-1 * rate.Traffic[j] * Traffic[j]))) -
      loggam(shape.Traffic)
    X.sim.Traffic[j] ~ dgamma(shape.Traffic, rate.Traffic[j])
    LLsim.Traffic_function[j] <- logdens.gamma(X.sim.Traffic[j], shape.Traffic, rate.Traffic[j]) # Log-likelihood for simulated data with your function
    LLsim.Traffic_manual[j] <- log((pow(rate.Traffic[j], shape.Traffic) *   # Log-likelihood for simulated data calculated manually by me
      X.sim.Traffic[j] * exp(-1 * rate.Traffic[j] * X.sim.Traffic[j]))) -
      loggam(shape.Traffic)
    #_______________#

  dev.obs.Traffic_function <- -2 * sum(LLobs.Traffic_function[1:ngrdyrs.hpresent])
  dev.sim.Traffic_function <- -2 * sum(LLsim.Traffic_function[1:ngrdyrs.hpresent])
  test.Traffic_function <- step(dev.sim.Traffic_function - dev.obs.Traffic_function) # GOF test with your function

  dev.obs.Traffic_manual <- -2 * sum(LLobs.Traffic_manual[1:ngrdyrs.hpresent])
  dev.sim.Traffic_manual <- -2 * sum(LLsim.Traffic_manual[1:ngrdyrs.hpresent])
  test.Traffic_manual <- step(dev.sim.Traffic_manual - dev.obs.Traffic_manual) # GOF test with my manual calculations
...

If I save "test.Traffic_function" and "test.Traffic_manual", they don't come out quite the same. I'm wondering if you (or anyone) is able to spot any errors in my manual calculations of the log-likelihood. If not, I can try to dig deeper (e.g., save the actual values from both log-likelihood calculations and compare).

