Subject: Inconsistencies between stick-breaking and CRP
Message-ID: <O9XSytRg8gw.GXC8WkVhBgAJ@nimble-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/nimble-users/c/O9XSytRg8gw/m/GXC8WkVhBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I am implementing a DPMM with random concentration parameter. The posterior for the concentration parameter seems to be different between the two approaches. If I bound the prior for the concentration parameter away from 0, the two approaches appear to be more consistent (perhaps it's a numerical issue?). Also, if I fix alpha to be small, the the results are more consistent. The issue appears to only happen when (1) the sample size is not huge; (2) the prior on alpha is bounded away from 0.

 I have attached a reproducible example.

